  {
    "id": "tables-multipage-tfoot-repeat",
    "category": "tables",
    "feature": "table-fragmentation",
    "subfeature": "tfoot-repeat",
    "description": "A long table with both <thead> and <tfoot> spanning pages: Chrome repeats the thead as a running header at the top and the tfoot as a running footer directly after the last body row at the bottom of every spanned page, reserving the footer height so body rows never collide with it. 320x240 page, 40px header+footer leave four 40px body rows per page; seven rows span TWO pages. Fails before the tfoot-repeat fix (footer shown once).",
    "file": "cases/tables/tables-multipage-tfoot-repeat.html",
    "kind": "feature",
    "expected_support": "implemented",
    "depends_on": [
      "probe-fill-box",
